<title>FINLAND: SOM SAYS FEB-JAN TRADE VOLUME UP 175 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>SOM SAYS FEB-JAN TRADE VOLUME UP 175 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade on the Finnish derivatives exchange Suomen Optiomeklarit Oy (SOM) in 12 months to end-January rose 175 percent year-on-year to 4.56 million contracts, SOM said in a statement on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The biggest index product brokers in January were Arctos</p>
<p>Securities in index options (16.8 percent), AG Private Bankers</p>
<p>in index futures (32.6 percent).</p>
<p>The biggest market maker in in index options and futures was</p>
<p>Alfred Berg Finland Oy (35.9 percent/30.5 percent).</p>
<p>In stock options, Arctos Securities was the biggest broker</p>
<p>(22.4 percent) in January and Alfred Berg was the biggest market</p>
<p>maker (55.9 percent).</p>
<p>AG Private Bankers was the biggest broker in stock futures</p>
<p>(52.6 percent), and Niles Trading was the biggest market maker</p>
<p>(26.4 percent).</p>
<p>SOM gave following statistics (number of contracts):</p>
<p>					  Feb 96-Jan 97  Feb 95-Jan 96</p>
<p>FOX options and futures		662,474	  695,234</p>
<p>STOX options and futures	   1,573,988	  782,503</p>
<p>LEX stock leasing contracts	  159,468	   12,846</p>
<p>FIM bond futures			 296,511	  140,280</p>
<p>FRA futures			    1,362,965	   18,685</p>
<p>FRX currency options and futures     6,525	    9,921</p>
<p>EL-EX futures			    498,642		n/a</p>
<p>Total				    4,560,573	1,659,469</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
